# fedora-dev .live-gate — the workload-shipped, self-describing host live-gate (Gate B) contract.
# ============================================================================
# PARSED — NEVER SOURCED — by the host's live-gate (live-gate-run.sh's lg_load reads this file
# line by line and assigns each KEY=VALUE with `printf -v`; it NEVER `.`/`source`s it, since this
# file travels in the UNTRUSTED PR head). Declare INERT KEY=VALUE pairs ONLY (one assignment per
# line, schema keys only, no cross-variable $OTHER refs). Single-quote HEALTH/PROBE so their inner
# $()/pipes run later INSIDE the fenced candidate (via --health-cmd / `podman exec`), never on the host.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: fedora-dev shipped no in-repo .live-gate, so the host fell back to a preset that
# only probed the SSH banner on :22 — proving the image builds + sshd serves, but NEVER that the
# claude-code self-update LOCKOUT (PR #45) actually holds after a real assemble. This contract closes
# that gap: it gives the eager first-boot claudebox assemble time to complete on the host, then proves
# the lockout is LIVE — `claude update` is disabled, and no native-build shadow sits on the home volume.
#
# Single default target. FENCE = run.sh's contract MINUS the public `-p` and MINUS real secrets/volumes
# (the nested-rootless-podman caps + devices + label-disable only). HEALTH mirrors run.sh's --health-cmd.
#
# NAMED DEFAULT-CAP CLOSURE (required): the host gate launches with a --cap-drop=ALL FLOOR and only
# adds back the caps this fence NAMES — but production `run.sh` runs under podman's IMPLICIT default
# cap set. So naming ONLY NET_ADMIN/SYS_ADMIN under-caps the candidate vs its own run-contract, and
# PID-1 dies at its first act: `cp -rT /etc/skel /home/core` + `chown -R core:core /home/core` need
# CHOWN/DAC_OVERRIDE/FOWNER; `runuser -u core` + sshd privsep need SETUID/SETGID/SETPCAP/SYS_CHROOT;
# the boot setcap restore needs SETFCAP; sshd:22 needs NET_BIND_SERVICE; the TERM-trap/watchdog needs
# KILL. PROVEN empirically (2026-07-07, in-box A/B): drop-ALL + the old 2 caps => candidate exits <1s
# at `cp: … Permission denied`; + this named default closure => boots, keys sync, assemble proceeds.
# This list = podman's default cap set, NAMED (a deliberate fence declaration, per the host validator's
# default-deny allowlist) + the run-contract's NET_ADMIN/SYS_ADMIN. (The host preset fedora-dev.env
# carries the same fix as the fallback, but this in-tree contract is authoritative and overrides it.)
CAND_FENCE='--cap-add CHOWN --cap-add DAC_OVERRIDE --cap-add FOWNER --cap-add FSETID --cap-add KILL --cap-add NET_BIND_SERVICE --cap-add SETFCAP --cap-add SETGID --cap-add SETPCAP --cap-add SETUID --cap-add SYS_CHROOT --cap-add NET_ADMIN --cap-add SYS_ADMIN --device /dev/net/tun --device /dev/fuse --security-opt label=disable'
HEALTH='pgrep -x sshd && pgrep -x tailscaled && test -S /run/user/1000/podman/podman.sock'

# Access-path probe (run INSIDE the candidate via `podman exec`): wait for the eager first-boot
# claudebox assemble, then assert PR #45's lockout LIVE —
#   (1) the box assembled (.assembled marker);
#   (2) NO native-build launcher shadow on the home volume (~/.local/bin/claude absent / self-healed);
#   (3) inside the assembled box, `claude update` is DISABLED — a LOCKED box prints
#       "...disabled by your administrator" (matches `grep -qi disabled`); an UNLOCKED RPM would
#       instead print "...managed by a package manager", which does NOT match → RED.
CAND_PROBE='for i in $(seq 1 72); do [ -e /home/core/.local/state/claudebox/.assembled ] && break; sleep 5; done; [ -e /home/core/.local/state/claudebox/.assembled ] && [ ! -e /home/core/.local/bin/claude ] && runuser -u core -- env XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/1000 podman exec claudebox bash -lc "claude update 2>&1 | grep -qi disabled"'

# Gate-imposed headroom + first-boot budget for the nested assemble (toolbox pull + dnf install
# claude-code ~244 MB) — more than a bare-sshd box; the probe itself also waits up to ~6 min for
# the .assembled marker.
CAND_MEMORY=4g
CAND_PIDS=2048
CAND_HEALTH_START=120s
CAND_HEALTH_TRIES=24
CAND_HEALTH_SLEEP=6
